A||N||14||MontanaFiero||"Mailing" a front facia...||||1||
Z||000000||MontanaFiero||04-14-2001||02:28 AM||||OK, so here it goes. I was down in Vegas and raided a few bone yards and came up with just about every body part I needed to complete my SE. The problem is now, due to unforseen circumstances, I am unable to get the facia home. (The other parts are on their way up in the trunk of a friend's car). Has anyone tried to mail one of these? The common carrier shipping company I called wanted $115 to get it here, and the damned thing can't weigh more than 25 pounds or so. Has anyone tried to put it on a greyhound bus, or perhaps someone has found a cheaper trucking company. <B>How much does a GT front facia weigh?</B> If I can get away with mailing it as oversized through the USPS, it should only cost about $20. ANY SUGGESTIONS??<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/blee291/fiero/mtfieroplate.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||pontiacs4me||04-14-2001||03:48 AM||||I tried to have one shipped from Oklahoma city to wichita kansas, and nobody would ship it.  UPS, USPS, fedex, only a freight truck would touch it, and they wanted more for shipping than the thing cost.  So I drove my dads van down there and picked it up myself.  <BR>BTW the box for it was custom made to perfectly fit it, and it was still way to big.||||reg||1
Z||000002||MontanaFiero||04-14-2001||04:25 AM||||Question... When the box was made, was it a rectangular box, or did the finished box wrap around like the bumper itself? In other words, did the box look like a "C"?||||reg||5
Z||000003||fyerstarter||04-14-2001||04:36 AM||||I have nothing to add except that I'm pissed because I could never find anything for my Fiero at the junkyards when I lived in Vegas :P||||reg||1
Z||000004||MontanaFiero||04-14-2001||04:45 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fyerstarter:<BR><B>I have nothing to add except that I'm pissed because I could never find anything for my Fiero at the junkyards when I lived in Vegas :P</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>This car that I found most of my parts from was a new arrival. And it was stacked on top of a couple of cars. I looked up and saw the wing, and said "Ummmm, could you get that car down for me?"<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||04-14-2001||07:05 AM||||its not the weight, its an oversized/odd shaped package. Its gonna cost you pretty hefty no matter how its sent and thats if you can find someone. I just got a Corvette nose from Ecklers in Fla, it came Federal Express, course I dont know how much. it came in a big rectangular box.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Old Lar||04-14-2001||09:07 AM||||Roger is right, the size does matter.  When I bought a nose from Fieroparts.com (aka Tim)he had a box for the nose that would be acceptable to the common carrier.  Now, the trick was that since the nose is quite flexible, the sides were "folded", not creased, into the nose so that it fit the box.  When I got it, I just let it come back to its original shape.||||reg||3
Z||000007||MrPBody||04-14-2001||09:10 AM||||I could be making this up, but . . .<P>As I recall, Ed Parks (The Fiero Factory) said that he ships fascias by US Postal Service.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||skitime||04-14-2001||10:54 AM||||I shipped with Greyhound. The size is not a problem and they are cheap. I shipped both front and rear facias, rocker panels and a bunch of other parts from Los Angeles to PA for $52. You can't beat that. <BR> <A HREF="http://206.66.2.229/" TARGET=_blank>http://206.66.2.229/</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||85Josh||04-14-2001||11:14 AM||||I just got a hood shipped to me from California, cost the guy $44.75. He used Greyhound.<P>------------------<BR>85 2M4(Lil' Bit)||||reg||1
Z||000010||MontanaFiero||04-14-2001||01:01 PM||||Hmmm, greyhound...<P>I work for the postal service, and I know I've seen some pretty big, odd things come through. It's just that the "mail manual" says it's too big.  But, if the sides really can be folded in without ruining it, it just might work.||||reg||1
Z||000011||danny boy||04-14-2001||04:38 PM|||| Ed Parks does ship fascias via USPS, and the funny thing is he does not box them. They won't ship in a box. I got mine and the mailing labels were on the Fascia. No Box.||||reg||1
Z||000012||MontanaFiero||04-15-2001||03:52 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by danny boy:<BR><B> Ed Parks does ship fascias via USPS, and the funny thing is he does not box them. They won't ship in a box. I got mine and the mailing labels were on the Fascia. No Box.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Actually, danny boy, me and some of the guys at work were talking about trying it that way. I'm wondering, did Ed re-inforce it some how?? or did he just mail it.||||reg||1
Z||000013||rogergarrison||04-15-2001||11:35 AM||||I did use US Postal service to ship a GT seat. I just wrapped it in cardboard and packaging tape. They charged $15 to Indianapolis. Also sent a set of Ferrari alloy wheels with tires to Massachusetts for $20 each, just put cardboard disk on faces with package tape.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 04-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000014||007DOUG||04-15-2001||03:18 PM||||I have shipped many facias through UPS. Cost about $23 each.<P>Facias are considered oversized for UPS. You might have problems getting it into the system. <P>Try using a Mail Boxes Etc. rather than the UPS customer counter.<P>Once in the system, an internal auditor could catch the package, and return it. But they are usually asleep. HINT: Think twice about what you write as your return address<P>I work for UPS, so I have no problem getting oversized packages into the system. I do not use a special box. I wrap the entire facia in cardboard. I have shipped as far as WA, and they have arrived undamaged.<P>I've shipped many front/rear facias, and trunklids via UPS with no problems. Although I'm still trying to get a hood though the system.<P>------------------<BR>5 Indy pace Cars (soon to be 7)<BR>84 T-top<BR>86 SE V6 157K (daily)<BR>86 GT red <BR>86 GT Yellow ASAP<BR>86 GT w/4:10 tranny<BR>86 GT 3.4 Pearl White T-top<BR>88 Formula 5 speed (soon)<BR>2 88 GT's (twins)<P>However......<BR><I>"Time is my most precious and most perishable of all my possessions."</I>||||reg||1
